PromoSlot database migrations (Alembic)
=======================================

Alembic is the single source of truth for the database schema. The app no
longer creates tables at import time — you bring a database up to date by
running migrations. The same migrations run on SQLite (dev) and Postgres
(prod); the target is chosen by the DATABASE_URL env var (see .env.example).

Common commands (run from the project root, with the venv active):

  alembic upgrade head          # create/upgrade the schema to the latest
  alembic current               # show the DB's current revision
  alembic history               # list revisions
  alembic downgrade -1          # roll back one revision

Changing the schema:

  1. Edit the SQLAlchemy models in backend/models.py.
  2. Autogenerate a migration:
         alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"
  3. Review the generated file in alembic/versions/ (autogenerate is a
     starting point, not gospel — check indexes, defaults, data moves).
  4. Apply it:
         alembic upgrade head

Notes:

- The URL comes from settings.database_url (DATABASE_URL) via alembic/env.py,
  so migrations always target whatever the app targets. The sqlalchemy.url in
  alembic.ini is only a fallback and is overridden at runtime.
- render_as_batch is enabled on SQLite so column ALTERs work there too; it is a
  no-op on Postgres.
- `alembic check` fails if the models have drifted from the latest migration —
  useful in CI to catch a model change that lacks a migration.
- Point DATABASE_URL at Postgres to run the exact same migrations there, e.g.
  DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://user:pass@host:5432/promoslot alembic upgrade head
